    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="1184" n="1079" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03mSupp/pg1079"/>

                <head>259. Letter From Gates to Goodpaster<anchor n="1" xml:id="d259-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-08-10">August 10, 1960</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear Andy:</salute>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d259-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d259-1"/>
                <p>I tabled this paper with the Joint Chiefs of Staff this afternoon, and it is the
                    subject we wish to cover with the President tomorrow morning at 10:15.</p>
                <p>In view of the fact that Admiral Burke is planning to attend to protest this
                    proposal, I felt you at least would want to read it first, and perhaps even
                    informally discuss it with the President prior to our arrival. I expect to
                    review the entire subject with the President when we arrive for our meeting.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Thomas S. Gates</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>







